#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521585} :activity/id #uuid "e3d9b7ec-1851-512a-a201-72d69471f1e2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049289 :topic/id #uuid "ea2533e0-c4a4-5c4e-b20a-9fb6ea3d7c70" :topic/math-academy-id 3231} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521585 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a76d935c-2199-5460-a09a-2ef79825d59f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521141}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521141} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bb8730e-04ca-5e0f-9b3a-6b1eb07a3311" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521348} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a14350e-8f1d-5034-8c34-0c1be5812523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520931}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520931} :answer-field/id #uuid "3420ffc8-c03a-5ee6-b400-0d64013fb521" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521354} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93049ccf-2b3b-5ef9-a326-d4f971a93e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521097}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521097} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e096f83-a268-52b6-a0de-9b2e3f7fae60" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d80de28b-ca2c-5fd8-ab88-370a0ca5902e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335606" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=3x(1-0.5x)-2xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-4y+4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. The equilibria of the model are the following:\n\n$(0,0),\\,(${{field-1}}$,0),\\,(${{field-2}}$,${{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x(1-0.5x)-2xy=0 \\\\ -4y+4xy=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4y+4xy & =0 \\\\ y(-4+4x) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y=0$ or $x=1.$ We consider both cases separately.\n\n- If $y=0,$ substituting it into the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x(1-0.5x)-2x(0) & =0 \\\\ 3x(0.5x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the first two equilibria are $(0,0)$ and $(2,0).$\n\n- If $x=1,$ substituting it into the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(1)(1-0.5(1))-2(1)y & =0 \\\\ 1.5-2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, another equilibrium is $(1,0.75).$\n\nTherefore, the equilibria of the model are\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(2,0),\\,(1,0.75).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2c4408e5-7391-59ee-b9e2-8bb13b7911cf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521586}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521586 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5945fd09-32e0-5f46-bbe0-b89a233c1a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520969}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520969} :answer-field/id #uuid "2df6522f-2c6e-54e2-92a8-830be048fc64" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ca83931-fb18-5c7d-b857-e2bfb9743388" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520939}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520939} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd1d7e76-9e39-5989-b9b2-3fd1ad45aa23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd513e1b-1d09-5226-9b47-696ee3a40809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521261}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521261} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4886f21-7c67-5733-a044-771bcc5c4cc0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3f73f08-cefc-5b56-bacc-8fec801a6a5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-335612" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x(1-0.05x)-3xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-4y+2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. The equilibria of the model are the following:\n\n$(0,0),\\,(${{field-1}}$,0),\\,(${{field-2}}$,${{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x(1-0.05x)-3xy=0 \\\\ -4y+2xy=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4y+2xy & =0 \\\\ y(-4+2x) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y=0$ or $x=2.$ We consider both cases separately.\n\n- If $y=0,$ substituting it into the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x(1-0.05x)-3x(0) & =0 \\\\ 2x(0.05x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the first two equilibria are $(0,0)$ and $(20,0).$\n\n- If $x=2,$ substituting it into the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)(1-0.05(2))-3(2)y & =0 \\\\ 3.6-6y & =0 \\\\ y & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, another equilibrium is $(2,0.6).$\n\nTherefore, the equilibria of the model are\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(20,0),\\,(2,0.6).\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2efaa86b-14b5-50a4-8011-f389ec1cb877" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521616}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521616 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c32c689-fe39-563b-8fe4-458134d4052b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "spiral sink" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370425} {:answer/id #uuid "d285e5c4-dc65-5536-9f79-3f681091c6e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "spiral source" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370426} {:answer/id #uuid "1c972551-9177-53db-ba32-aadf4301d9d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "saddle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370427} {:answer/id #uuid "a46f4309-ae1e-5db4-a422-01ee70908e05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370428}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370427} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8765f0e-22b2-5636-ab04-0200c2dfbf11" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37be5f91-8fed-5a74-8252-d9a7770dbee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370430} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b06cef-c0d0-5cc3-83a5-153945337c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370431} {:answer/id #uuid "96937e62-b165-5f11-b02d-20c826e17e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370432} {:answer/id #uuid "385807c1-d661-5815-b158-0fdbe8f65bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370433} {:answer/id #uuid "d9cb3226-d4ec-57d4-a311-0033515fa357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370434}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370433} :answer-field/id #uuid "38813121-32ea-57cc-90d9-3045a8865